+# Design Report — <TICKET>: <Short Title>
+
+## Context
+
+_Resolved once in Frame. Every later phase reads these values instead of re-resolving them. Two-track deployments: see `patterns/context-resolution.md`. Single-track deployments: these are fixed values, filled in once._
+
+## State
+
+```yaml
+current_stage: frame
+completed_stages: []
+selected_artifacts: []
+next_action: ""
+context_fingerprint: ""
+```
+
+Update this block whenever a phase starts, completes, or is invalidated. The
+`selected_artifacts` values are interface names (`architecture`, `design`, `stack`,
+`efforts`) and are the source of truth for downstream review, publish, and resume.
+
+## Evidence
+
+| Source | Read at stage | Relevant decision or constraint | Reference/version |
+| ------ | ------------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------- |
+
+Record every required or relevant context source actually read. Add conflicts and
+their resolution here; do not rely on conversation history for design provenance.
+
+| Field               | Value                                                                                                  |
+| ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
+| Track               | <Product / Project — Two-track only; omit this row for single-track deployments>                       |
+| Source docs         | <{{DESIGN_DOCS_ROOT}}>                                                                                 |
+| Dest docs           | <{{DESIGN_DOCS_ROOT}}{subfolder}>                                                                      |
+| Subfolder           | <resolved subfolder/section>                                                                           |
+| Architect agent     | <{{DESIGN_ARCHITECT_AGENT}}>                                                                           |
+| Implementation note | <resolved implementation note — where the resulting tickets are typically implemented; Two-track only> |
